  "text": {
    "paragraphs": [
      "Teacher Kim has a big box. \"It has hats and jackets,\" she says. \"Today we are animals!\" Mia has a gray jacket. \"I am an elephant,\" says Mia. Leo has a yellow hat. \"I am a duck!\" says Leo. Lily has a brown hat. \"I am a donkey,\" says Lily. The children stand in a line.",
      "\"Where is the elephant?\" asks Teacher Kim. \"I am next to the door,\" says Mia. \"Where is the duck?\" asks Teacher Kim. \"I am behind Mia,\" says Leo. \"What color is the donkey's hat?\" \"It is brown,\" says Lily. \"What color is Leo's hat?\" asks Mia. \"It is yellow!\" says Lily. Pip comes to the door. Pip looks.",
      "\"What is Pip?\" asks Teacher Kim. \"He is a dog,\" says Leo. \"He wants a jacket,\" says Lily. Teacher Kim has a small red jacket. She puts it on Pip. Pip stands between the duck and the donkey. \"Woof!\" says Pip. \"We have four animals,\" says Teacher Kim. The children clap."
    ],
    "summary": "Teacher Kim has a box of hats and jackets for an animal play. The children say where they are and what color their clothes are, and Pip gets a red jacket.",
